diff --git a/specs/003-patch-conformance/spec.md b/specs/003-patch-conformance/spec.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7bb2b26183ee9af49bf8a3a7d08790e137747159
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/003-patch-conformance/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+# Spec: applyPatch conformance review (RFC 6902 sections 3, 4, 5)
+- A patch is validated in full before any operation is applied, so an invalid operation is reported as
+  `JsonPatchInvalidError` even when an earlier operation would fail (section 5: error, no effect).
+- Holes in a sparse patch array are invalid operations, not skipped.
+- `op` is read only as an own member of the operation object.
+Tests: tests/patch.test.ts ("whole patch is validated before applying...").
